"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[92424],{792424:n=>{n.exports='# How to time range\n\n## When to use `pageUpdateLakewatchQueryTimeRange`\n\nUse it when the user wants to change the **query’s global time filter** (the DateTimeRangePicker).\n\n**Do not** use it for time conditions inside SQL/WHERE on result columns — use query refinement instead.\n\n## Format: ISO 8601 only\n\nAlways set `timeRangeDescription` to **one** shape:\n\n```text\n<start> to <end>\n```\n\n- **`<start>`** and **`<end>`** are full ISO 8601 **instants**: date, `T`, time, and timezone (`Z` for UTC or `+hh:mm` / `-hh:mm`).\n- Put the word **`to`** between them (spaces around `to`). Do not use other separators in `timeRangeDescription`.\n\n**You** interpret what the user meant (“last week”, “past hour”, “Q1 2025”, “today”, etc.), choose concrete start/end moments (usually in UTC unless the user specified a zone), and **pass only this ISO range** — not natural-language shortcuts.\n\nExamples of valid `timeRangeDescription` values:\n\n- `2025-01-01T00:00:00Z to 2025-12-31T23:59:59Z`\n- `2025-05-01T00:00:00Z to 2025-07-01T23:59:59Z`\n- `2026-03-14T12:00:00Z to 2026-03-21T12:00:00Z` (rolling week ending “now”, if you computed those instants from current time)\n\nDo **not** pass date-only pairs (`YYYY-MM-DD to YYYY-MM-DD` without `T`…), English month/day strings, or phrases like `last month` as the tool input.\n\n## Tool shape\n\n```json\n{\n  "thoughts": "What the user wanted and how you mapped it to start/end instants (e.g. UTC).",\n  "timeRangeDescription": "<ISO instant> to <ISO instant>"\n}\n```\n\n## Errors\n\nIf parsing fails, fix the string: both bounds must be full instants with `T` and a timezone; then retry.\n'}}]);
